{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_transports_transport", "label": "Transport interface", "file_type": "code", "rationale": "A deliberately small surface \u2014 bootstrap, send, receive, disconnect \u2014 so cluster behavior is identical no matter which implementation is plugged in.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/transports.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_transports_tcptransport", "label": "TcpTransport", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/transports.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_transports_inmemorytransport", "label": "InMemoryTransport", "file_type": "code", "rationale": "A process-global registry keyed by NodeAddress routes frames between in-process transports, which is what lets MultiNodeSpec spin up a multi-node cluster in one process; it simulates neither failures, latency, nor serialization.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/transports.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_transports_tcpbackend", "label": "TcpBackend", "file_type": "code", "rationale": "TcpTransport never talks to the OS directly; one backend per runtime (Bun.listen, node:net, Deno.listen) is auto-detected so the same transport works everywhere.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/transports.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_transports_frame_size_cap", "label": "Per-frame size cap", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Frames larger than the cap (16 MiB default) are rejected to prevent a denial of service via a faked length prefix; raising it does not improve general throughput.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/transports.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_transports_multiplexing", "label": "Transport multiplexing", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Gossip, heartbeats, envelopes and subsystem traffic share one TCP stream with no priority routing, so isolating cluster control bandwidth needs a custom transport with per-channel framing.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/transports.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_transports_readiness_check", "label": "cluster-transport readiness check", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "peers() backs the readiness probe: a node with expected members and no connection to any of them is cut off and answers 503 so a load balancer stops routing to it. InMemoryTransport reports every registered transport regardless of connection state, so a test written against it cannot observe the check failing.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/transports.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_transports_custom_transport", "label": "Custom transport", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The interface is small enough for roughly 200 lines; the difficulty is matching the framing and heartbeat semantics the cluster expects.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/transports.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_transports_messagechanneltransport", "label": "MessageChannelTransport", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/transports.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url"